1
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:11,733
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:32,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,733
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:40,967
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:41,933 --> 00:00:43,800
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,100
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:46,633
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:48,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:50,967
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:53,600
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,233
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,967
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:57,967 --> 00:01:00,100
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:03,000
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:04,567 --> 00:01:06,000
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,033 --> 00:01:09,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,533
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:12,667
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,667 --> 00:01:14,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,800
<i>This is the CCTV footage
of the safe house.</i>

21
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:23,667
<i>That damn bastard.
Who are you?</i>

22
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:25,200
<i> Did you sign the document?</i>

23
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,000
I can't pass up the opportunity
<i> to have a lot of money.</i>

24
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,200
<i>What should I do
to make Rudy sign?</i>

25
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,433
<i>Since they already see me
as a bad person,</i>

26
00:01:34,433 --> 00:01:36,133
<i>I'll show them
just how evil I can be.</i>

27
00:01:37,033 --> 00:01:39,233
<i>- (In Japanese) Hello.
- That'll do.</i>

28
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:41,133
<i> I'm sorry for lying to you.</i>

29
00:01:41,167 --> 00:01:43,433
<i>I just can't tell you
about my mission.</i>

30
00:01:43,433 --> 00:01:45,267
<i>I should be taking
this opportunity</i>

31
00:01:45,267 --> 00:01:46,633
<i> to find out the truth.</i>

32
00:01:46,633 --> 00:01:48,900
<i>But I'm becoming closer to him
than expected.</i>

33
00:01:55,933 --> 00:02:02,867
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

34
00:02:07,667 --> 00:02:09,033
You're early.

35
00:02:10,033 --> 00:02:11,233
Why are you drinking?

36
00:02:11,233 --> 00:02:12,233
[BETCHAY SNIFFLES]

37
00:02:12,233 --> 00:02:14,800
I was thinking
about what I did yesterday.

38
00:02:15,433 --> 00:02:16,600
I'm ashamed.

39
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:19,900
I hope you can forgive me.

40
00:02:21,467 --> 00:02:22,800
I'm sorry.

41
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:25,967
I should be making you happy.

42
00:02:26,567 --> 00:02:32,400
But it seems I lost
my confidence to do that.

43
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:39,333
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

44
00:02:39,767 --> 00:02:40,700
'Dy.

45
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:43,533
I'm sorry.

46
00:02:44,933 --> 00:02:47,567
I'm really sorry.
please forgive me.

47
00:02:49,233 --> 00:02:50,233
[BETCHAY INHALES]

48
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,567
I love you so much.

49
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:56,067
Don't forget that.

50
00:02:56,967 --> 00:03:02,267
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

51
00:03:02,267 --> 00:03:03,433
Alright, fine.

52
00:03:04,833 --> 00:03:05,867
Come on.

53
00:03:06,933 --> 00:03:07,867
Let's sleep.

54
00:03:09,933 --> 00:03:10,900
That's enough.

55
00:03:11,633 --> 00:03:12,600
'Dy.

56
00:03:14,867 --> 00:03:16,133
I wanted to...

57
00:03:17,133 --> 00:03:18,967
...celebrate your birthday

58
00:03:18,967 --> 00:03:21,167
since I couldn't do it
yesterday.

59
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,767
Can we celebrate
with just the two of us,

60
00:03:23,767 --> 00:03:25,233
just like before?

61
00:03:26,133 --> 00:03:27,167
[RUDY INHALES]

62
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:30,100
Please?

63
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:32,100
Alright.

64
00:03:32,733 --> 00:03:33,700
[GLASS THUDS]

65
00:03:34,467 --> 00:03:36,833
No, no, no, 'Dy.
Sit beside me.

66
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:39,800
Come on!

67
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:41,900
[RUDY GROANS]

68
00:03:43,833 --> 00:03:45,767
- [BOTTLE CLINKS]
- [ALCOHOL POURING]

69
00:03:45,767 --> 00:03:46,867
That's enough.

70
00:03:46,867 --> 00:03:49,600
[BETCHAY] But we're celebrating.
You should have more.

71
00:03:50,367 --> 00:03:51,667
Bottoms up!

72
00:03:51,667 --> 00:03:52,700
[GLASSES CLINK]

73
00:03:53,267 --> 00:03:54,600
Happy birthday!

74
00:03:54,633 --> 00:03:56,067
- [BETCHAY CHUCKLES]
- [GLASSES CLINK]

75
00:03:56,067 --> 00:04:00,900
[SNEAKY MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:01,900
Good, right?

77
00:04:03,167 --> 00:04:04,200
Right, 'Dy?

78
00:04:06,367 --> 00:04:07,300
Yeah.

79
00:04:08,767 --> 00:04:11,067
'Dy, something's missing.

80
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:14,000
- Huh?
- Something is missing.

81
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,467
We don't have food.

82
00:04:16,333 --> 00:04:17,833
Do we still have corned beef?

83
00:04:20,067 --> 00:04:21,533
- I think so.
- Alright!

84
00:04:22,167 --> 00:04:24,533
Can we eat that, please?

85
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:32,867
[SNEAKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:04:33,433 --> 00:04:39,267
[CUTLERY CLATTERING]

87
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:44,433
[PLASTIC BAG RUSTLING]

88
00:04:45,967 --> 00:04:52,467
[SNEAKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

89
00:04:52,467 --> 00:04:54,467
[CUTLERY CLATTERING]

90
00:04:54,467 --> 00:04:55,967
[ALCOHOL POURING]

91
00:04:55,967 --> 00:04:59,467
- [CUTLERY CLATTERING]
- [BOTTLE THUDS]

92
00:04:59,467 --> 00:05:02,333
[FORK CLATTERING]

93
00:05:02,367 --> 00:05:03,333
Here.

94
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,867
That's it!

95
00:05:07,367 --> 00:05:08,367
[BETCHAY GROANS]

96
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:11,200
[CUTLERY CLINKING]

97
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:13,267
This was our favorite
back then, right?

98
00:05:13,267 --> 00:05:16,067
When we have money, this was
the first thing we bought.

99
00:05:16,067 --> 00:05:17,467
- Mm-hmm.
- Have a drink.

100
00:05:17,933 --> 00:05:18,900
[CUTLERY CLINKS]

101
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,133
I'm sure you got tired.

102
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,300
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

103
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:24,633
You got tired from preparing
the corned beef.

104
00:05:24,633 --> 00:05:25,633
Drink more!

105
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:29,267
Cheers!
[SINGING]  Happy birthday, 'Dy

106
00:05:29,267 --> 00:05:32,233
<i> Happy birthday, 'Dy</i>

107
00:05:32,933 --> 00:05:34,100
[BETCHAY MOANS]

108
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,267
[RUDY EXHALES]

109
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,233
That was good, wasn't it?

110
00:05:42,167 --> 00:05:43,467
- Sir.
- [KAREN] Sir.

111
00:05:43,467 --> 00:05:46,233
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:05:46,233 --> 00:05:48,933
[DELGADO] Team Alpha,
I know this might be...

113
00:05:50,467 --> 00:05:53,067
...our most depressing day
at work.

114
00:05:55,867 --> 00:05:58,333
You treated Sam like a sibling.

115
00:05:58,333 --> 00:06:03,733
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

116
00:06:03,733 --> 00:06:06,000
Guys, I believe we have to...

117
00:06:06,833 --> 00:06:08,267
...pay our respects to Sam.

118
00:06:08,967 --> 00:06:13,000
I'll ask Aunt Isobel
for the details

119
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,567
about their memorial service
for Sam.

120
00:06:16,333 --> 00:06:17,800
Don't bother, Tuazon.

121
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,633
We're not allowed
to go there.

122
00:06:20,633 --> 00:06:22,833
That is Gen. Jacinto's order.

123
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:24,933
So we can't pay our respects?

124
00:06:24,933 --> 00:06:27,867
I already expected
the Jacintos' anger.

125
00:06:27,867 --> 00:06:29,067
But, sir.

126
00:06:29,067 --> 00:06:31,567
We're not responsible
for Sam's death.

127
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:32,800
The Zafras are!

128
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:36,700
We have to respect
the decision of the family.

129
00:06:37,333 --> 00:06:38,300
Team Alpha...

130
00:06:40,433 --> 00:06:41,500
Let it go.

131
00:06:43,733 --> 00:06:44,800
Soldier on.

132
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:52,333
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

133
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:10,033
[MUSIC FADES]

134
00:07:10,033 --> 00:07:10,933
[SALVADOR] Ma'am.

135
00:07:12,767 --> 00:07:19,300
We'd just like to confirm
the death of an NCIA agent.

136
00:07:21,567 --> 00:07:23,633
- What's going on?
- Oh, madam.

137
00:07:23,633 --> 00:07:25,433
- Good evening!
- [OLI] Good evening, madam.

138
00:07:25,433 --> 00:07:30,267
We'd like to ask
about Agent Samantha Jacinto.

139
00:07:30,267 --> 00:07:32,400
If she's dead?

140
00:07:33,267 --> 00:07:34,600
Yeah, she's dead!

141
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:37,500
But they've yet to...

142
00:07:38,667 --> 00:07:40,367
Well, they didn't find her body.

143
00:07:40,367 --> 00:07:42,433
Ma'am, she's dead?

144
00:07:42,433 --> 00:07:46,367
Last we heard,
she was on leave.

145
00:07:46,367 --> 00:07:47,367
Leave?

146
00:07:49,267 --> 00:07:51,567
Maybe they meant
she left the Earth.

147
00:07:54,067 --> 00:07:56,200
You know, it's even sad

148
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:59,800
because, although we want
to pay our respects,

149
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:03,900
Gen. Jacinto forbade us
from going to her wake.

150
00:08:04,433 --> 00:08:05,600
Where's the wake, anyway?

151
00:08:06,267 --> 00:08:08,600
If I'm not mistaken,
it'll be in their house.

152
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:10,767
There's no corpse.

153
00:08:12,167 --> 00:08:13,333
So it'll just be there.

154
00:08:21,533 --> 00:08:22,567
[GLASS THUDS]

155
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,733
'Dy?

156
00:08:27,933 --> 00:08:29,133
Hm?

157
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:31,000
Do you still love me?

158
00:08:32,767 --> 00:08:33,733
What?

159
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:36,533
[CUTLERY CLINKING]

160
00:08:37,133 --> 00:08:40,367
If you love me,
then can I get a kiss?

161
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,333
Even just one will do.

162
00:08:43,967 --> 00:08:45,900
Come on, 'Dy.

163
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,733
Just one kiss.

164
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:50,800
'Dy?

165
00:08:52,467 --> 00:08:55,467
[SLOW ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

166
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:58,467
[MUSIC TURNS SNEAKY]

167
00:08:58,467 --> 00:09:00,367
'Dy? Hey, 'Dy!

168
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:04,800
Rudy? Rudy!

169
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,100
[SLAPS BACK]

170
00:09:09,467 --> 00:09:16,467
[SNEAKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

171
00:09:20,567 --> 00:09:21,600
[BETCHAY INHALES]

172
00:09:22,567 --> 00:09:23,567
Stay right there.

173
00:09:23,567 --> 00:09:26,133
[OBJECTS CLATTER]

174
00:09:26,133 --> 00:09:30,800
[ENVELOPE RUSTLING]

175
00:09:31,767 --> 00:09:34,700
[PAPER RUSTLING]

176
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,067
[ENVELOPE RUSTLES]

177
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:45,733
[SNEAKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:09:45,733 --> 00:09:46,633
Ah.

179
00:09:50,033 --> 00:09:55,500
[PEN NIB RUSTLING]

180
00:09:58,033 --> 00:09:59,133
[SLAMS TABLE]

181
00:09:59,133 --> 00:10:04,600
[SNEAKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

182
00:10:04,633 --> 00:10:07,533
[PEN SCRIBBLING]

183
00:10:18,833 --> 00:10:20,333
[SNEAKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:10:20,333 --> 00:10:21,533
[GIGGLES QUIETLY]

185
00:10:23,533 --> 00:10:24,967
[WHISPERS] Don't move!

186
00:10:24,967 --> 00:10:26,167
I've got to be quick!

187
00:10:27,167 --> 00:10:28,333
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]
- Okay.

188
00:10:28,967 --> 00:10:29,967
One more.

189
00:10:29,967 --> 00:10:31,533
Hold your thumb up.

190
00:10:31,533 --> 00:10:32,500
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

191
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:36,233
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

192
00:10:37,067 --> 00:10:38,100
[PHONE THUDS]

193
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:40,033
[SNEAKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

194
00:10:40,033 --> 00:10:41,000
[ENVELOPE RUSTLES]

195
00:10:43,767 --> 00:10:48,567
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

196
00:10:48,567 --> 00:10:49,933
- [HEAVY THUD]
- [MUSIC FADING]

197
00:10:58,833 --> 00:10:59,867
[BETCHAY SIGHS IN RELIEF]

198
00:10:59,867 --> 00:11:06,800
[SNEAKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

199
00:11:19,667 --> 00:11:24,900
[PHONE BUZZING]

200
00:11:24,967 --> 00:11:27,267
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:11:27,267 --> 00:11:28,333
Hello?

202
00:11:28,833 --> 00:11:30,067
Miss Betchay?

203
00:11:30,067 --> 00:11:31,533
<i> Hello, Miss Beautiful.</i>

204
00:11:31,533 --> 00:11:34,533
Sorry, I'm calling late.

205
00:11:34,533 --> 00:11:36,067
No, it's okay.

206
00:11:36,067 --> 00:11:37,333
What made you call?

207
00:11:37,333 --> 00:11:39,200
I just wanted
to tell you that...

208
00:11:39,633 --> 00:11:42,200
I finally got Rudy to sign.

209
00:11:42,867 --> 00:11:44,067
<i> He was totally game.</i>

210
00:11:44,067 --> 00:11:45,233
He agreed right away.

211
00:11:45,233 --> 00:11:47,033
I've got proof.

212
00:11:47,033 --> 00:11:49,467
Miss Betchay,
thank you very much.

213
00:11:49,467 --> 00:11:51,233
Okay, I'll pick it up
from there right away.

214
00:11:51,233 --> 00:11:52,233
<i> Alright.</i>

215
00:11:52,233 --> 00:11:54,367
I'm here in Ginintuang Lupa.

216
00:11:54,367 --> 00:11:56,867
Just text me when you're close.

217
00:11:56,867 --> 00:11:58,667
Sure thing. Thanks again.

218
00:11:58,667 --> 00:12:05,600
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

219
00:12:06,567 --> 00:12:10,200
[BETCHAY] <i> Now I'm definitely
</i> going to be rich.

220
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:15,567
[MUSIC SWELLING]

221
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,633
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

222
00:12:16,633 --> 00:12:18,000
[MUSIC FADES]

223
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,200
- Miss?
- Uh...

224
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,667
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

225
00:12:23,133 --> 00:12:24,233
Have you been there long?

226
00:12:24,533 --> 00:12:26,367
Not really. I just stepped out.

227
00:12:26,367 --> 00:12:27,533
Where are you going?

228
00:12:27,533 --> 00:12:29,133
To the restroom.

229
00:12:29,133 --> 00:12:31,033
Mister Rudy already fell asleep.

230
00:12:31,033 --> 00:12:34,233
[SCOFFS] We were drinking.
He's weak, see?

231
00:12:34,233 --> 00:12:35,367
Totally knocked out.

232
00:12:35,367 --> 00:12:37,733
He couldn't handle his alcohol,
unlike Paquito.

233
00:12:37,733 --> 00:12:39,867
Come on, let's bring him
to his room.

234
00:12:39,867 --> 00:12:41,633
[BETCHAY] Oh, no, no.
I'm not drunk yet.

235
00:12:41,633 --> 00:12:44,500
I'll wake him up later
for another round.

236
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:46,800
Just go on with your business.

237
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,100
Alright.

238
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:54,200
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

239
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:58,500
[BETCHAY] <i> Did she hear my
</i>phone call with Miss Beautiful?

240
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,333
<i> I might get caught here.</i>

241
00:13:01,333 --> 00:13:04,600
<i>But she said she didn't see
or hear anything.</i>

242
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:06,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

243
00:13:06,867 --> 00:13:13,033
<i>If the truth ever comes out,
I'll make sure she regrets it.</i>

244
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:18,067
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

245
00:13:19,367 --> 00:13:20,333
Go back to sleep.

246
00:13:20,333 --> 00:13:21,767
- I'll take care of him.
- Okay.

247
00:13:26,267 --> 00:13:30,667
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

248
00:13:30,667 --> 00:13:34,100
[BETCHAY] <i> You can keep
</i>your worthless principles, Rudy.

249
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:36,433
<i> As for me,</i>

250
00:13:37,067 --> 00:13:38,767
<i> I will rise above this life.</i>

251
00:13:39,267 --> 00:13:43,033
<i> I refuse to die still poor.</i>

252
00:13:43,033 --> 00:13:44,667
<i> The problem with you</i>

253
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:47,167
is you don't know how to dream,

254
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:50,267
<i> you don't know how to hustle,</i>

255
00:13:50,767 --> 00:13:53,367
<i>you're not willing to do
whatever it takes</i>

256
00:13:53,367 --> 00:13:55,433
<i> to climb out of this pit.</i>

257
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:57,233
<i> I'm different.</i>

258
00:13:57,600 --> 00:14:00,767
<i> I will do everything</i>

259
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:04,067
<i> to get out of this hellscape.</i>

260
00:14:04,767 --> 00:14:07,833
<i>Of all the men
I could have loved,</i>

261
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:11,333
<i> why did it have to be you?</i>

262
00:14:14,067 --> 00:14:21,067
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

263
00:14:25,467 --> 00:14:28,267
[SAM] <i> I wonder what piece
</i>of paper Miss Betchay's holding.

264
00:14:29,067 --> 00:14:33,100
<i>And why does it feel like
she's hiding something?</i>

265
00:14:35,467 --> 00:14:36,800
<i> Maybe not.</i>

266
00:14:37,267 --> 00:14:40,600
<i>Maybe she really is having
a good time with Mister Rudy.</i>

267
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,567
<i> I hope they finally get along,</i>

268
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:47,633
and that she treats Gabo better
<i> from now on.</i>

269
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:56,233
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

270
00:15:11,067 --> 00:15:15,500
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

271
00:15:16,033 --> 00:15:17,167
Well, guys?

272
00:15:18,067 --> 00:15:19,200
Wanna hang out at my place?

273
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:20,733
I feel like having
a drink right now.

274
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,400
I'm down.

275
00:15:24,733 --> 00:15:30,567
I want to drown out
this pain and heartbreak.

276
00:15:30,867 --> 00:15:31,967
What do you say, Karen?

277
00:15:31,967 --> 00:15:33,067
Reyes? Bullet?

278
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:34,500
No thanks.

279
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:35,500
I'll sit this one out.

280
00:15:36,633 --> 00:15:38,433
How about you, Borromeo?
Come on, join us.

281
00:15:38,433 --> 00:15:39,400
Count me out.

282
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,500
I'll pass for now.

283
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,267
What's the matter with you guys?

284
00:15:42,267 --> 00:15:43,467
We're not doing this
just because

285
00:15:43,467 --> 00:15:45,233
we're grieving Sam's death.

286
00:15:45,233 --> 00:15:46,467
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

287
00:15:46,467 --> 00:15:48,600
We're doing this
for our team too.

288
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:49,933
Come on, guys.

289
00:15:51,067 --> 00:15:52,367
We all know that Sam
wouldn't want

290
00:15:52,367 --> 00:15:53,533
to see us sad like this.

291
00:15:53,533 --> 00:15:55,533
She wouldn't want
to see us like this,

292
00:15:55,533 --> 00:15:56,600
falling apart.

293
00:15:57,067 --> 00:15:58,167
Bullet's right.

294
00:15:58,167 --> 00:16:01,867
You know, lately I've noticed
tensions between us.

295
00:16:02,367 --> 00:16:04,600
I don't even know why, but...

296
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,067
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

297
00:16:06,067 --> 00:16:07,867
I think we all need this.

298
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:08,900
Right?

299
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:11,533
To fix things
and come together again.

300
00:16:12,667 --> 00:16:14,067
So we can...

301
00:16:14,067 --> 00:16:17,533
...figure out how to carry
our team forward.

302
00:16:17,533 --> 00:16:18,667
Remember this.

303
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:20,367
We owe it to Sam.

304
00:16:20,367 --> 00:16:23,867
Honestly, team,
maybe finding Sam's jacket...

305
00:16:23,867 --> 00:16:26,567
...is what can guide us
to reunite.

306
00:16:26,567 --> 00:16:30,700
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

307
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,133
[DOOR CLOSES]

308
00:16:33,133 --> 00:16:34,500
[SALVADOR GROANS]

309
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:38,467
If the wake will be held
at General Jacinto's house,

310
00:16:38,467 --> 00:16:40,267
how can we even get there?

311
00:16:40,267 --> 00:16:44,867
Even though the village guards
tried to drag us out before,

312
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:46,067
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

313
00:16:46,067 --> 00:16:48,567
we'll still find a way.

314
00:16:48,567 --> 00:16:50,100
- How?
- Hmm...

315
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:52,233
You know very well everyone
recognizes my face by now.

316
00:16:52,767 --> 00:16:55,000
They'll surely spot me.
Come on now.

317
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,067
[LAUGHS]

318
00:16:56,067 --> 00:16:57,133
Dude!

319
00:16:57,667 --> 00:16:59,167
Leave it to Oli!

320
00:16:59,167 --> 00:17:00,600
I've got a plan.

321
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:06,267
I know exactly how we can get
to General Jacinto's house

322
00:17:06,267 --> 00:17:09,100
and once we're there,

323
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:13,500
the next episode will be bigger

324
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:17,500
than any headline.

325
00:17:18,533 --> 00:17:20,233
[LOW CHUCKLE]

326
00:17:25,567 --> 00:17:27,667
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

327
00:17:27,667 --> 00:17:28,767
[BETCHAY WHISPERS]
Miss Beautiful!

328
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:31,600
We'll talk here!

329
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:33,067
This way!

330
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:38,700
[DOG BARKING IN DISTANCE]

331
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:39,900
Psst! Attorney!

332
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:41,333
Keep an eye out!

333
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:44,133
[EXHALES LOUDLY]

334
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:46,633
Attorney.

335
00:17:46,633 --> 00:17:49,900
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

336
00:17:49,933 --> 00:17:53,067
[ENVELOPE RUSTLING]

337
00:17:53,067 --> 00:17:55,000
[GASPING]

338
00:17:55,967 --> 00:17:56,967
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

339
00:17:56,967 --> 00:17:58,667
[ENVELOPE RUSTLING]

340
00:17:58,667 --> 00:18:00,700
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

341
00:18:02,067 --> 00:18:03,067
Here.

342
00:18:04,867 --> 00:18:08,400
[ENVELOPE RUSTLING]

343
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:10,700
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

344
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:11,867
Attorney, please check.

345
00:18:11,867 --> 00:18:13,500
So you keep your word,
Miss Beautiful.

346
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:14,767
- [MAX] Of course.
- [CHUCKLES]

347
00:18:20,033 --> 00:18:22,767
See? I told you
I could pull it off.

348
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:27,933
I trust you, Miss Betchay.

349
00:18:28,233 --> 00:18:29,467
- I'll send these to you.
- Send them to me.

350
00:18:29,467 --> 00:18:31,200
Here you go,
I'm sending them now.

351
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,200
Check it.

352
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:35,367
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

353
00:18:35,367 --> 00:18:36,433
Good job.

354
00:18:36,433 --> 00:18:37,433
[MUSIC FADES]

355
00:18:37,433 --> 00:18:39,167
Alright then, Miss Betchay.
We'll leave now.

356
00:18:39,167 --> 00:18:41,400
Wait, wait, wait.
Hang on, Miss Beautiful.

357
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:42,800
Can we...

358
00:18:43,133 --> 00:18:46,867
...keep this between us?

359
00:18:46,867 --> 00:18:48,933
- Sure.
- No one else should know, okay?

360
00:18:49,267 --> 00:18:53,133
What we discussed should just
stay between the two of us.

361
00:18:53,133 --> 00:18:54,933
Absolutely, Miss Betchay.
It's our little secret.

362
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:56,000
Why?

363
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:59,000
Won't you tell
the neighbors that...

364
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,333
...you sold them off?

365
00:19:01,367 --> 00:19:02,367
[SNICKERS]

366
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:04,567
Of course.

367
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,633
Listen here, Miss Beautiful...

368
00:19:06,633 --> 00:19:08,467
If they find out about this,

369
00:19:08,467 --> 00:19:10,167
both of us will be in trouble.

370
00:19:10,633 --> 00:19:13,733
Remember, you bribed me.

371
00:19:14,433 --> 00:19:16,233
You can count on me,
Miss Betchay.

372
00:19:16,633 --> 00:19:17,967
We're in agreement, then.

373
00:19:19,467 --> 00:19:20,533
Bye-bye, Miss Beautiful.

374
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:22,567
Attorney, hold me.

375
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:25,667
- I might fall.
- Take care, Miss Betchay.

376
00:19:25,667 --> 00:19:26,700
You too.

377
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:30,367
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

378
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:31,700
[SIGHS]

379
00:19:34,433 --> 00:19:36,467
[MAX] <i> For the price
</i> of one million pesos,

380
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:38,900
she's willing to offer her soul.

381
00:19:43,967 --> 00:19:48,367
[DOGS BARKING IN DISTANCE]

382
00:19:48,367 --> 00:19:49,900
This place is truly awful.

383
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:53,900
Dark, cramped, hot.

384
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:56,100
The people make me sick!

385
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:58,000
I don't want
to stay here anymore!

386
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,467
One day,

387
00:19:59,467 --> 00:20:03,267
I'll get out of this place.

388
00:20:04,067 --> 00:20:06,533
Out of this ugly place.

389
00:20:07,633 --> 00:20:08,667
I don't belong here.

390
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:12,600
I can't believe it.

391
00:20:13,767 --> 00:20:15,567
It's so hard to accept that
Ma'am Sam is gone.

392
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:17,867
I'm going to miss her.

393
00:20:17,867 --> 00:20:19,333
She was an excellent leader.

394
00:20:20,433 --> 00:20:23,300
She was smart,
compassionate,

395
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,467
and knew how to listen,

396
00:20:24,533 --> 00:20:26,600
and this is what the Zafras
did to her.

397
00:20:28,333 --> 00:20:29,500
Did we fail her?

398
00:20:30,333 --> 00:20:32,000
Was there something else
we could've done

399
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,300
to prevent this?

400
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:34,667
No.

401
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:37,233
We did everything
we could to find her.

402
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,300
But we were just too late.

403
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:47,633
We'll make it up to her.

404
00:20:47,633 --> 00:20:49,433
We need to get justice for Sam.

405
00:20:49,933 --> 00:20:51,100
How?

406
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:54,100
We need to get justice
for her death.

407
00:20:54,100 --> 00:20:57,300
We need to hold the people
who did this accountable.

408
00:20:57,300 --> 00:21:00,700
Everyone who's responsible
will pay for what they did.

409
00:21:00,767 --> 00:21:03,467
You know, Castor was right.

410
00:21:03,833 --> 00:21:05,467
We need to stand united.

411
00:21:06,633 --> 00:21:08,200
I know...

412
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:09,600
we have our differences.

413
00:21:09,633 --> 00:21:12,400
But we need to put
our grudges aside.

414
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,633
Don't you agree?

415
00:21:14,133 --> 00:21:20,967
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

416
00:21:24,767 --> 00:21:26,367
Let's do this for Sam.

417
00:21:26,367 --> 00:21:28,467
Let's solve her murder

418
00:21:28,467 --> 00:21:30,933
and the last case she handled.

419
00:21:32,167 --> 00:21:33,233
For Sam.

420
00:21:33,233 --> 00:21:34,667
- For Sam!
- For Sam!

421
00:21:35,833 --> 00:21:42,700
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

422
00:21:57,600 --> 00:22:04,433
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

423
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:07,667
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

424
00:22:11,533 --> 00:22:18,400
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

425
00:22:32,567 --> 00:22:39,433
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

426
00:22:43,233 --> 00:22:44,300
[MUSIC FADES]

427
00:22:46,233 --> 00:22:53,200
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

428
00:23:17,433 --> 00:23:19,433
"Gabo, we're expecting you."

429
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:27,033
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

430
00:23:31,867 --> 00:23:34,000
We need to be careful
about who we ask.

431
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:35,800
We don't know
if they're protecting

432
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:37,567
the person we're looking for.

433
00:23:39,500 --> 00:23:41,233
What are we going
to tell people?

434
00:23:41,233 --> 00:23:43,167
The important thing is,

435
00:23:43,167 --> 00:23:45,867
they can't figure out that
we're looking for someone.

436
00:23:45,867 --> 00:23:49,133
Because once that person
finds out we're after him,

437
00:23:49,133 --> 00:23:50,933
they'll go into hiding.

438
00:23:50,933 --> 00:23:53,700
Right now, what's important
is that we're looking for a man

439
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:55,133
with long hair who rides
a motorcycle.

440
00:23:55,167 --> 00:23:56,667
They don't need to know that.

441
00:23:56,667 --> 00:23:59,033
So whatever information we have,
we keep it to ourselves.

442
00:23:59,033 --> 00:24:00,800
Just between the two of us?

443
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:02,500
We won't even tell Colonel?

444
00:24:03,433 --> 00:24:05,567
If we tell Colonel Domingo,

445
00:24:05,567 --> 00:24:07,700
the gold will end up
in evidence again.

446
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:09,967
Aren't we the ones
looking for it?

447
00:24:09,967 --> 00:24:11,633
Then we're the ones
who should take it.

448
00:24:11,633 --> 00:24:15,133
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

449
00:24:29,633 --> 00:24:36,467
[MUSIC BECOMES UNSETTLING]

450
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:57,500
Honey?

451
00:24:59,133 --> 00:25:00,267
Honey.

452
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,267
Honey.

453
00:25:09,333 --> 00:25:10,533
Hey.

454
00:25:11,600 --> 00:25:12,833
You're leaving already?

455
00:25:13,500 --> 00:25:14,700
Yeah, honey.

456
00:25:14,700 --> 00:25:17,667
I'm heading out to look
for a job.

457
00:25:17,667 --> 00:25:19,167
Wait.
Is that what you're wearing?

458
00:25:20,233 --> 00:25:21,467
Yeah.

459
00:25:21,467 --> 00:25:22,633
Didn't you say last night

460
00:25:22,633 --> 00:25:25,433
that I needed to dress
properly and look formal?

461
00:25:25,433 --> 00:25:27,133
This is the nicest outfit
I have.

462
00:25:27,133 --> 00:25:28,200
That won't do.

463
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:30,733
You need to look decent
and presentable.

464
00:25:30,733 --> 00:25:32,233
That's not going to help you
get hired.

465
00:25:32,233 --> 00:25:34,800
And your hair...
you really need a haircut.

466
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:36,200
Hey, not the haircut.

467
00:25:36,233 --> 00:25:37,633
I can't get a haircut.

468
00:25:37,633 --> 00:25:39,400
If I cut it, I might lose
my strength.

469
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:40,633
This is my source of power.

470
00:25:40,633 --> 00:25:43,067
And my sex appeal
looks better like this.

471
00:25:43,067 --> 00:25:45,433
Gabo, you need
to look presentable.

472
00:25:45,433 --> 00:25:47,167
No one's going to hire you
looking like that.

473
00:25:47,167 --> 00:25:48,733
You need to get a haircut.

474
00:25:49,333 --> 00:25:52,833
Honey, just tell me
what you want.

475
00:25:52,833 --> 00:25:55,500
I'll do anything, just don't
make me cut my hair.

476
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:56,800
It took me so long
to grow it out.

477
00:25:56,800 --> 00:25:58,833
I've had it this long since
I was a kid, and then...

478
00:25:58,833 --> 00:26:00,200
Gabo, you need to get
a haircut.

479
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:01,200
I'll just make breakfast,

480
00:26:01,200 --> 00:26:02,700
then you're getting
that haircut.

481
00:26:02,700 --> 00:26:03,933
Hey, wait.

482
00:26:03,933 --> 00:26:06,233
I'll cook instead.

483
00:26:06,233 --> 00:26:07,533
Don't get up.

484
00:26:07,533 --> 00:26:09,700
Get some more sleep.
I'll take care of everything.

485
00:26:09,733 --> 00:26:10,767
No, it's fine.

486
00:26:10,767 --> 00:26:12,300
I'll just change my clothes.

487
00:26:12,300 --> 00:26:13,767
Then I'll find something
for you to wear.

488
00:26:13,767 --> 00:26:15,367
You can't wear that.

489
00:26:16,367 --> 00:26:17,400
Honey, come on.

490
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:20,533
[GABO] Jeez!

491
00:26:21,100 --> 00:26:26,867
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

492
00:26:28,667 --> 00:26:30,600
Boss, here's what you
asked me to buy.

493
00:26:33,133 --> 00:26:35,533
Is this the same one
Mariano gave us to drink?

494
00:26:35,533 --> 00:26:36,733
The imported one?

495
00:26:36,733 --> 00:26:38,200
I don't want the
local stuff anymore.

496
00:26:38,867 --> 00:26:41,400
Your taste sure gets fancy
when you have money, boss.

497
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:43,133
Of course!

498
00:26:43,133 --> 00:26:45,533
Once you've had
the expensive stuff,

499
00:26:45,533 --> 00:26:47,233
you can't go back
to the cheap stuff.

500
00:26:47,233 --> 00:26:49,000
[LAUGHTER]

501
00:26:49,533 --> 00:26:50,633
Open it already.

502
00:26:51,033 --> 00:26:52,100
Let's go.

503
00:26:55,833 --> 00:26:58,533
Whether it's alcohol or food,

504
00:26:58,533 --> 00:27:01,600
or even women, we can't settle
for just anything anymore.

505
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:03,033
[LAUGHTER]

506
00:27:03,033 --> 00:27:05,167
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

507
00:27:08,500 --> 00:27:09,800
Smooth.

508
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:10,933
Another one!

509
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:12,767
[CHUCKLING]

510
00:27:13,833 --> 00:27:16,867
Gloria's definitely
going to love this.

511
00:27:16,900 --> 00:27:18,200
She'll be dazzled by it.

512
00:27:18,900 --> 00:27:21,267
And I'll finally be able to
take her away from Gabo.

513
00:27:21,267 --> 00:27:23,133
- [CHUCKLING]
- But, boss,

514
00:27:23,700 --> 00:27:25,067
as long as Gabo's around,

515
00:27:25,067 --> 00:27:27,100
you won't be able
to have Gloria.

516
00:27:27,100 --> 00:27:29,367
That's why I'm finding a way

517
00:27:29,367 --> 00:27:31,933
to get rid of that bastard Gabo.

518
00:27:31,933 --> 00:27:34,100
[SINISTER CHUCKLE]

519
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:38,867
Any news from the NLEA?

520
00:27:38,867 --> 00:27:40,433
Haven't they caught Gabo yet?

521
00:27:41,567 --> 00:27:42,633
Not yet.

522
00:27:42,633 --> 00:27:44,633
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

523
00:27:47,500 --> 00:27:48,700
Papa.

524
00:27:50,100 --> 00:27:51,400
Why did you sleep here?

525
00:27:52,500 --> 00:27:53,533
Hey, Gabo.

526
00:27:54,533 --> 00:27:55,833
Uhm...

527
00:27:55,833 --> 00:27:58,067
Your Mama Betchay
and I were drinking.

528
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,567
Then I suddenly blacked out.

529
00:28:02,033 --> 00:28:03,867
I don't remember
what happened after that.

530
00:28:03,867 --> 00:28:05,533
Why drink when
you couldn't even handle it?

531
00:28:05,533 --> 00:28:08,133
Why didn't Mama Betchay
move you to the bedroom?

532
00:28:08,133 --> 00:28:09,300
Are you okay?

533
00:28:09,700 --> 00:28:10,800
I'm okay.

534
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:12,833
But what exactly happened to me?

535
00:28:12,833 --> 00:28:14,200
- Uh...
- Who drank this?

536
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:17,833
Aunty, Papa and Mama Betchay
were drinking last night.

537
00:28:17,833 --> 00:28:19,700
You two are talking now?
What a miracle.

538
00:28:19,700 --> 00:28:22,133
No, no. It's not like that.

539
00:28:22,167 --> 00:28:25,600
I came out of the bedroom
and saw Betchay drinking alone.

540
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:27,733
- [MAMENG] Then?
- I felt sorry for her,

541
00:28:27,733 --> 00:28:29,300
so I joined her.

542
00:28:30,300 --> 00:28:32,500
What were you two
talking about this time?

543
00:28:32,500 --> 00:28:33,833
Nothing, really.

544
00:28:34,500 --> 00:28:36,833
It's just that I noticed...

545
00:28:36,833 --> 00:28:39,733
Betchay seemed different.

546
00:28:39,733 --> 00:28:40,933
Can you believe it?

547
00:28:40,933 --> 00:28:42,667
She even apologized to me.

548
00:28:43,300 --> 00:28:46,300
She said she was sorry for
what she did on my birthday.

549
00:28:46,300 --> 00:28:48,567
Well, maybe she finally
thought about

550
00:28:48,567 --> 00:28:50,933
the things she said to us.

551
00:28:50,933 --> 00:28:53,933
Maybe she wants to
turn her life around.

552
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,433
I sure hope so.

553
00:28:56,700 --> 00:28:58,000
Wait a minute.

554
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:00,633
Why are you dressed like that?
Where are you going?

555
00:29:01,500 --> 00:29:03,467
Aunty, don't you remember?

556
00:29:03,467 --> 00:29:05,167
I'm applying for a job today.

557
00:29:05,167 --> 00:29:09,133
Gloria said I need
to dress properly

558
00:29:09,133 --> 00:29:10,467
and look presentable.

559
00:29:10,467 --> 00:29:13,700
You really need to find a job,

560
00:29:13,700 --> 00:29:15,533
especially after
all that practice

561
00:29:15,533 --> 00:29:17,300
- you and Gloria did last night.
- You were so good.

562
00:29:17,300 --> 00:29:18,533
Don't worry!

563
00:29:18,533 --> 00:29:21,167
I'm ready for anyone
who interviews me.

564
00:29:21,167 --> 00:29:23,333
What we practiced last night?
Easy!

565
00:29:23,333 --> 00:29:24,700
You really were good.

566
00:29:24,700 --> 00:29:26,633
- Good morning.
- Hey.

567
00:29:26,633 --> 00:29:28,333
Oh, look, Gloria!

568
00:29:28,333 --> 00:29:29,500
Take a look at this.

569
00:29:29,533 --> 00:29:33,233
My nephew's all ready
to look for a job!

570
00:29:33,233 --> 00:29:34,667
Yes, Aunty.

571
00:29:34,667 --> 00:29:36,800
But he still hasn't gotten
a haircut.

572
00:29:38,133 --> 00:29:41,167
Oh, Gabo.
Your wife already told you.

573
00:29:41,167 --> 00:29:43,767
Get a haircut. Come on.

574
00:29:43,767 --> 00:29:44,933
Aunty...

575
00:29:44,933 --> 00:29:47,833
You know I've hated getting
haircuts since I was a kid.

576
00:29:47,833 --> 00:29:49,300
This is my source of strength.

577
00:29:49,300 --> 00:29:51,500
What if I get a haircut
and lose my strength?

578
00:29:51,500 --> 00:29:53,733
Then that could be the reason
I don't get hired.

579
00:29:53,733 --> 00:29:55,400
You told me last night

580
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:57,600
you'd do everything
I told you to do,

581
00:29:57,600 --> 00:29:59,800
especially during
your interview.

582
00:29:59,800 --> 00:30:02,133
Gabo, come on.
Get a haircut.

583
00:30:02,167 --> 00:30:03,767
Listen to your wife.

584
00:30:04,500 --> 00:30:08,033
Honey, please.
Come on, give me this one.

585
00:30:08,033 --> 00:30:10,633
No.
You need to get a haircut.

586
00:30:11,533 --> 00:30:13,667
- Papa...
- Listen to your wife.

587
00:30:14,733 --> 00:30:15,900
[MAMENG] Come on.

588
00:30:15,900 --> 00:30:22,300
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

589
00:30:22,733 --> 00:30:24,733
<i> Gabo needs formal clothes.</i>

590
00:30:24,733 --> 00:30:26,400
<i> I don't have money to buy any.</i>

591
00:30:26,400 --> 00:30:28,567
<i>If you want,
we can hustle for some money.</i>

592
00:30:28,567 --> 00:30:29,933
<i>- No!
- Fight!</i>

593
00:30:29,933 --> 00:30:32,733
<i>I haven't made him feel like
I truly see him as my daughter.</i>

594
00:30:32,733 --> 00:30:34,900
<i>Now, I'm asking
for a second chance.</i>

595
00:30:34,900 --> 00:30:36,067
<i> Just come back to us, Sam.</i>

596
00:30:36,100 --> 00:30:38,233
<i>Let me show you
how much I love you.</i>

597
00:30:38,233 --> 00:30:40,167
<i>Didn't you say you were
looking for a long-haired man?</i>

598
00:30:40,167 --> 00:30:42,200
<i>Long hair and rides
a motorcycle.</i>

599
00:30:42,200 --> 00:30:43,300
<i> We found him.</i>

600
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:44,633
<i> They need to get to Gabo.</i>

601
00:30:44,633 --> 00:30:46,767
<i>If they do,
he'll end up in prison again.</i>

602
00:30:46,767 --> 00:30:48,767
<i> And Gloria will be mine.</i>
